# Event log

The event table is the only record. Projections are rebuilt from events by a Postgres fold. Fix a projection by rebuilding it from events, not by editing history.

## Writes

- Insert only. No client `UPDATE` or `DELETE` policy on `events` or on projection tables.
- Unique `(stream_id, version)` for optimistic concurrency. A version conflict is retried by the command, not patched.
- Each event has `org_id`, `stream_id`, `stream_type`, `version`, `event_type`, `schema_version`, `payload`, `actor_id`, `occurred_at`.
- Postgres folds events into projections. Application code does not `UPDATE` projection tables.

## Insert trigger and grants

A `BEFORE INSERT` trigger on `events`:

- sets `actor_id` from `auth.uid()` for a user JWT, or from the role session setting for `horizon_writer` and `horizon_ci`
- ignores any `actor_id` in the payload
- rejects an `event_type` that `event_type_grants` does not grant to the current role

The service role has no grant rows, so the trigger rejects its runtime inserts. WP-01 owns the trigger and the grants table. Later packages insert grant rows and their own projection migrations; they do not edit the trigger.

## Streams (phase 1)

`organization`, `membership`, `proposal`, `decision`, `check`, `research_session`, `harness`, `pull_request`

Name events in past-tense PascalCase (`DecisionProposed`) and set `schema_version`.

## Grants

| Role | Event types |
|---|---|
| member (`authenticated`) | `ResearchSessionOpened`, `DiscussionNoted` |
| `horizon_writer` | `ProposalCreated`, `ProposalVerified`, `DecisionProposed`, `PullRequestReceived` |
| `horizon_ci` | `CheckRecorded`, `ProposalCreated` of kind `review_violations` only |
| `approve_proposal` / `reject_proposal` | `ProposalApproved` or `ProposalRejected`, plus the one domain event the kind names |

`OrganizationCreated` and `MemberAdded` are seed and admin writes, not member inserts.

## Where a command runs

The web client appends only member-granted event types. Branching logic, model calls, and commands that touch more than one stream go through `services/agent`, which writes as `horizon_writer`.

```sql
-- ❌ projection is not the source of truth
update public.decisions set status = 'accepted' where id = '...';

-- ✅ append the fact; the projection follows (actor_id is set by the trigger)
insert into public.events (
  org_id, stream_id, stream_type, version, event_type, schema_version, payload
) values (
  '...', '...', 'decision', 1, 'DecisionProposed', 1, '{"adr_id":"ADR-001"}'
);
```

## Proposals

`ProposalCreated` → `ProposalVerified` → `approve_proposal` or `reject_proposal`.

`approve_proposal` appends `ProposalApproved` and the domain event for the kind (`DecisionAccepted`, `DecisionSuperseded`, or `HarnessCompiled`) in one transaction. A direct insert of those event types fails the trigger — neither the browser nor `horizon_writer` can append them. `DiscussionNoted` is not approval.
